Resistance Training Volume Enhances Muscle Hypertrophy but Not Strength in Trained Men

Paper Metadata
This randomized controlled trial investigated how different weekly resistance-training volumes affect muscle hypertrophy, strength, and muscular endurance in resistance-trained men. Participants trained for 8 weeks using identical exercises and repetition ranges while performing either 1, 3, or 5 sets per exercise. The study primarily examined whether increasing training volume produces greater muscular adaptations in trained lifters.



